  "worked_solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2z-4 & =2z+1 \\\\ 2z-4-2z & =2z+1-2z \\\\ -4 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $z.$ Therefore, the equation $2z-4=2z+1$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5z+6 & =5z+6 \\\\ 5z+6-5z & =5z+6-5z \\\\ 6 & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $z.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3z+2 & =z+4 \\\\ 3z+2-z-2 & =z+4-z-2 \\\\ 2z & =2 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $3z+2=z+4$ has the unique solution $z=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
